			How to compile Edutella:

1.  Download ARP2 as part of Jena2 from
http://jena.sourceforge.net/downloads.html or from
http://user.it.uu.se/~udbl/software/Jena-2.1.zip

2. Set environment variable ARP2_HOME to point to Jena 2 root directory,
   e.g. C:\Program\Jena-2.1

3. Make sure your javac compiler has version 1.4 or later!

   In your default Java is 1.3 or earlier it is possible to override
   the default setting by assigning the interface variable JAVA_HOME
   to the directory where javac.exe etc. are defined, e.g.  
     set java_home=C:\Program\Java\jdk1.5.0_01\bin\

4. Make pselo.dmp by running
     mkdmp.cmd

6. Test Edutella by
     test.cmd

7. Run Edutella by
     run.cmd

Note! Edutella can also be tested in PSELO  mode,that is, 
QEL queries are executed over union of statement sources defined in stmt() fn.

For this to work the user machine must have the right to penetrate the firewall of Museifönstret. 
Also MSSQL 2000 JDBC driver must be downloaded from 
http://udbl.it.uu.se/software/MSSQL 2000 driver SP1.zip

Environment variable MSSQL_HOME should point to MSSQL 2000 JDBC driver root directory,
e.g. C:\Program\MSSQL 2000 driver SP1

Now Edutella could be run or tested with argument 'pselo' for this more advanced mode of execution. 
e.g. 
C:\data\AmosNT\embeddings\Edutella>run pselo







    
   